population with age due to mortality.  This is unlike the smoothed data which follows a linear decline
with age. Age groups 5-9 and 35-39 for males as well as age groups 5-9 and 15-19 for females create
a ‘bulge’ in the age distribution, which is unexpected.
The data in Table 6.1 also reveal positive and negative differences by age and sex between the
enumerated and smoothed data, which to a large extent are due to the magnitude of errors in age
reporting.  Age group 0-4 for males, for example, suggests a difference of 58,575 between the
reported and the smoothed data; or an increase of 12.5 per cent.  Overall the smoothing process
reveals that half of the age groups experienced an increase, whilst another half recorded a decrease
in population.
Source: Statistics Sierra Leone, 2015 Population and Housing Census
