A population pyramid reflecting the smoothed data is presented in Figure 6.4. The characteristic
features of this pyramid are:
a) The peaks are truncated at age 75+.
b) The population 0-4 years has now become the broadest segment for both sexes as expected.
c) There is a consistent decline in population with age, as is expected.
6.3.1 Comparison between reported and smoothed data by age and sex for Sierra
Leone
In Figures 6.5 and 6.6 the reported age data by age and sex are compared with the smoothed data
to underline the extent of differences or similarities between the two curves. Regarding the males,
there are more similarities than differences. The reported data are to a large extent consistent with
the smoothed data, especially from age group 15-19 and beyond.  This is attributed to better age
reporting among the males.
In Figure 6.6, there are wide disparities between the reported and smoothed data.  The gap is widest
at the younger ages and narrows as age increases.  This result emphasizes the point made earlier
that age reporting among females is less accurate than among males.
